 "note": "Two columns joined on each line, separated by reading order. Left column: MIDDLE SCHOOL STAFF (Continued) (line 1) -> middle (printed 'Middle School'); MIDDLE SCHOOL AIDES (23: Okerman) -> middle; ELEMENTARY SCHOOL STAFF (27: Feinberg, Forrest, Freeman, Hallfors, Lowe, Milliken, Weller, Normandin) -> passios (bare 'Elementary School' = Passios, inferred from other pages; several of these have K-5 roles that span the Primary School too, kept passios because the heading is Elementary). Dr. Rose M. Feinberg, Director of Reading (K-12) and Language Arts (K-8), -> district-wide. Right column: P.L. 89-10 TITLE I TEACHERS (line 1: Colello, Van Horne; no building printed -> unknown) then ELEMENTARY TEACHERS (Continued) (line 7), grades 5A..2E -> passios. Headings share lines 1, 7, 23 and 27 with entries or continuation text. Position lines under names are ignored; role_raw carries them. Willingham (line 45, right column) has no position printed; Niemi's note says she replaced Ms. Willingham in Grade 2C; Milliken's and Weller's roles are on lines 45 and 48. Maki Grade 5B note: TRANSFERRED from Special Needs Dept 1/5/81 (also on p115). Honorifics: this page prints none other than Dr. Line 57 page number. Integration pass, 31 Oct 2026: school bus contractors, drivers and volunteers moved from entries to ignored (not school staff; every 1971-1980 page treated alike), and `middle` written `turkey-hill` -- the 1972 and 1974 listings print the building as `Turkey Hill Middle School (Grades 5-7)`, the town's one middle school."
